---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { loadCatalog } from '../lib/catalog'
import { formatDateTime, formatNumber } from '../lib/format'

const catalog = await loadCatalog()
const { snapshot } = catalog
---

<Base
  title="About and sources"
  description="Catalog data sources, freshness policy, curated identity data, free-offer rules and known gaps."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">About this catalog</p>
    <h1>Sources, freshness and limits</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This is a separate, static catalog. It is not the Shepherd agent pool, does not expose a
      runtime database and does not publish private account data.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="detail-grid">
    <section class="card">
      <h2>Snapshot</h2>
      <dl class="detail-list">
        <div><dt>Snapshot id</dt><dd><code class="mono">{snapshot.snapshotId}</code></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Schema</dt><dd>v{snapshot.schemaVersion}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Generated</dt><dd>{formatDateTime(snapshot.generatedAt)}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Source refreshed</dt><dd>{formatDateTime(snapshot.sourceFetchedAt)}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Stale after</dt><dd>{formatDateTime(snapshot.freshnessDeadline)}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Age</dt><dd>{snapshot.ageDays.toFixed(1)} days</dd></div>
        <div>
          <dt>Stale</dt>
          <dd>
            {
              snapshot.stale
                ? 'Yes — values may have changed since the snapshot'
                : 'No — inside the seven-day window'
            }
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Sources and license</h2>
      {
        snapshot.sources.length === 0 ? (
          <p>No source row is recorded in this snapshot.</p>
        ) : (
          <div class="table-wrap">
            <table>
              <caption class="visually-hidden">Data sources recorded in this snapshot</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Source</th>
                  <th scope="col">License</th>
                  <th scope="col">Fetched</th>
                  <th scope="col">Response</th>
                  <th scope="col">Checksum</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {snapshot.sources.map((source) => (
                  <tr>
                    <td>
                      <a href={source.sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
                        {source.name}
                      </a>
                      <div class="small muted">{source.attribution}</div>
                    </td>
                    <td>{source.license}</td>
                    <td>{formatDateTime(source.fetchedAt)}</td>
                    <td>
                      HTTP {source.httpStatus ?? 'unknown'} · {source.status}
                      {source.error && <div class="small muted">{source.error}</div>}
                    </td>
                    <td>
                      <code class="mono" title={source.contentSha256}>
                        {source.contentSha256.slice(0, 12)}…
                      </code>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        )
      }
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What is in this snapshot</h2>
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value">{formatNumber(catalog.providers.length)}</span><span class="stat__label">providers</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value">{formatNumber(catalog.models.length)}</span><span class="stat__label">model entries</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value">{formatNumber(catalog.canonicalModels.length)}</span><span class="stat__label">canonical models</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value">{formatNumber(catalog.families.length)}</span><span class="stat__label">families</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value">{formatNumber(catalog.harnesses.length)}</span><span class="stat__label">harnesses</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value">{formatNumber(catalog.benchmarks.length)}</span><span class="stat__label">benchmark definitions</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value">{formatNumber(catalog.plans.length)}</span><span class="stat__label">plans</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><span class="stat__value">{formatNumber(catalog.offers.length)}</span><span class="stat__label">recurring offers</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Facts, identity and sources</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <p>
        Provider and model facts come from the public models.dev catalog, and every row keeps the
        source URL and source record it was read from. The catalog does not publish a per-fact
        verification status: a snapshot is the observation, and its age is shown above.
      </p>
      <p>
        Canonical model identity correlates the same release across providers. models.dev supplies
        a canonical id for most rows; the rest are derived from the wire id, and a canonical model
        is the join point for benchmark scores.
      </p>
      <p>
        Harness links, the family tree and benchmark definitions are curated in the catalog
        package. They are reviewed data, sourced where a public source exists, not inferred from a
        model name alone.
      </p>
      <p>
        Benchmark scores are keyed by canonical model, so one score covers every provider serving
        that release. No score is published until a benchmark source is enabled; an unknown score
        stays unknown.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Free-offer policy</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <p>
        A free offer is published only when a provider documents a recurring allowance with a
        defined unit and reset period. Launch credits, one-time signup grants, expiring trials and
        unverified community claims are excluded.
      </p>
      <p>
        A zero token price is a model price, not a recurring free offer. Unknown allowance or reset
        information stays unknown; this catalog does not estimate it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Known gaps in this snapshot</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <ul>
        {snapshot.knownGaps.map((gap) => <li>{gap}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p>
        The catalog also does not yet have an approved source for subscription plans, recurring
        free allowances or local runtime hardware. Those tables are intentionally empty rather
        than guessed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Freshness and failure</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <p>
        This snapshot was generated {formatDateTime(snapshot.generatedAt)} from source data fetched
        {formatDateTime(snapshot.sourceFetchedAt)}. It is treated as stale after
        {formatDateTime(snapshot.freshnessDeadline)}; from then on a warning banner appears, but the
        values remain visible instead of disappearing or being guessed.
      </p>
      <p>
        A failed scrape does not overwrite the previous snapshot. It leaves a failure record, and
        the previous snapshot stays buildable. If a provider or model disappears from a later
        response it is retained and flagged as retained for review rather than deleted.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is generated from a DuckDB snapshot at build time. There is no public query API,
        scraper endpoint or runtime database.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
